# Correction Task: Merge Text Generation + Image Analysis Into One Tab with Visible Queue

## Found
The previous task redesigned the **standalone** `ImageAnalyzerWindow.xaml` — a separate window that is NOT the main UI. The user's main UI is `ImageGeneratorWindow.xaml`, which uses a `TabControl` with tabs. The "Text Generation" tab (line 229) and "Image Analysis" tab (line 671) inside `ImageGeneratorWindow` were **never modified**, so none of the queue UI or input mode toggle changes are visible.

## Fix Required
Merge the "Text Generation" and "Image Analysis" tabs into **one unified tab** inside `ImageGeneratorWindow.xaml`, and add the queue system UI to this merged tab.

---

## 1. Context & Architecture

- **Main window:** `ImageGeneratorWindow.xaml` — has a `TabControl` starting at line 225
- **Tab 1 ("Text Generation"):** Lines 229-668. Binds directly to `ImageGeneratorViewModel` properties (`ImagePrompt`, `SelectedWorkflow`, `AspectRatioIndex`, `Steps`, `Cfg`, `GenerateImageCommand`, etc.)
- **Tab 2 ("Image Analysis"):** Lines 671-1037. Binds to `Analyzer.*` properties (the nested `ImageAnalyzerViewModel`)
- **`ImageGeneratorViewModel`** already has its own queue system: `_promptQueue` (ObservableCollection<ImagePromptQueueItem>), `AddToQueueCommand`, `RemoveFromQueueCommand`, `ClearQueueCommand`, `ProcessQueueCommand`, `PauseQueueCommand`, `ResumeQueueCommand`
- **`ImageAnalyzerViewModel`** (nested as `Analyzer`) also has a queue system with `QueueItems`, `AddToQueueCommand`, etc.

The **Text Generation** features (saved prompts, direct text prompt, workflow selection, LoRA, generate) and **Image Analysis** features (browse image, QwenVL analysis, edit prompt, generate) must be combined.

## 2. Files to Modify

### `FlipPix.UI/ImageGeneratorWindow.xaml`
This is the ONLY file that needs changes. The ViewModel code is already in place from the previous task.

### Files to reference (DO NOT modify):
- `FlipPix.UI/ImageAnalyzerWindow.xaml` — Use as reference for the queue UI design (Sections E-H)
- `FlipPix.UI/ViewModels/ImageGeneratorViewModel.cs` — Understand available bindings
- `FlipPix.UI/ViewModels/ImageAnalyzerViewModel.cs` — Understand `Analyzer.*` bindings

## 3. Implementation Steps

### Step 1: Remove Tab 2 ("Image Analysis") entirely
Delete lines 670-1037 (the entire `<TabItem Header="🔍 Image Analysis">` block).

### Step 2: Redesign Tab 1 into a merged "Image Generator" tab
Replace the current "Text Generation" tab (lines 229-668) with a new unified tab. The new tab header should be `"🎨 Image Generator"`.

**Layout:** Use a 2-column grid layout inside a ScrollViewer:

#### LEFT COLUMN (~50% width) — Input & Settings

**Section A: Input Mode Toggle**
- Two styled RadioButtons as toggle: `[ Text Prompt ]` / `[ Image Analysis ]`
- Use `Analyzer.IsTextPromptMode` and `Analyzer.IsImageAnalysisMode` bindings (these were added in the previous task)

**When "Text Prompt" is selected:**
- Show the Saved Prompts section (currently in Text Generation tab, lines 239-282). Keep bindings as-is (`SavedPrompts`, `SelectedSavedPrompt`, `SavePromptCommand`, `DeletePromptCommand`)
- Show the large prompt TextBox bound to `ImagePrompt`
- Show example prompts (lines 300-312)

**When "Image Analysis" is selected:**
- Show the image browse/preview area bound to `Analyzer.SourceImagePath`, `Analyzer.BrowseImageCommand`, `Analyzer.SourceImageSource`, `Analyzer.HasSourceImage`
- Show "Analyze Image with QwenVL" button bound to `Analyzer.AnalyzeImageCommand`
- Show analyzing progress (bound to `Analyzer.IsAnalyzing`)
- Show the prompt TextBox bound to `Analyzer.AnalysisText` (analysis result goes here, user can edit)

**Section B: Workflow & Settings (always visible, below the toggle sections)**
- Workflow selection ComboBox: `SelectedWorkflow` binding for Text Prompt mode, `Analyzer.SelectedWorkflow` for Image Analysis mode. **Simplification:** Since both use the same workflows, bind to `SelectedWorkflow` (ImageGeneratorViewModel's property) when in Text Prompt mode. When in Image Analysis mode, bind to `Analyzer.SelectedWorkflowIndex`.
- Actually, keep it simple: Use TWO separate settings panels, one for each mode, controlled by the same visibility toggle. This avoids complex binding switching.
  - **Text Prompt settings** (visible when `Analyzer.IsTextPromptMode`): Keep the existing bindings (`SelectedWorkflow`, `AspectRatioIndex`, `Steps`, `Cfg`, `LoraEnabled`, `SelectedLora`, etc.)
  - **Image Analysis settings** (visible when `Analyzer.IsImageAnalysisMode`): Keep the existing `Analyzer.*` bindings (`Analyzer.SelectedWorkflow`, `Analyzer.AspectRatioIndex`, `Analyzer.Steps`, `Analyzer.Cfg`, etc.)

**Section C: Action Buttons**
- For **Text Prompt** mode (visible when `Analyzer.IsTextPromptMode`):
  - "Generate Image" button → `GenerateImageCommand`
  - "Add to Queue" button → `AddToQueueCommand`
  - "Add to Queue & Start" button (adds + starts processing)
- For **Image Analysis** mode (visible when `Analyzer.IsImageAnalysisMode`):
  - "Generate Image" button → `Analyzer.GenerateImageCommand`
  - "Add to Queue" button → `Analyzer.AddToQueueCommand`
  - "Add to Queue & Start" button → `Analyzer.AddToQueueAndStartCommand`

#### RIGHT COLUMN (~50% width) — Queue & Results

This column shows queue status and results. Since Text Prompt mode uses `ImageGeneratorViewModel`'s queue and Image Analysis mode uses `Analyzer`'s queue, show the appropriate one based on mode.

**For Text Prompt mode** (visible when `Analyzer.IsTextPromptMode`):

**Queue Status Bar:**
- Show counts using `ImageGeneratorViewModel` queue properties
- Processing progress bar when `IsProcessingQueue` is true

**Queue Items List:**
- `ItemsControl` bound to `PromptQueue`
- Each item shows: workflow badge, truncated prompt, status, progress, remove button
- Use the same visual pattern as the `ImageAnalyzerWindow.xaml` queue list (Sections E-H)

**Queue Controls:**
- Process Queue → `ProcessQueueCommand`
- Clear Queue → `ClearQueueCommand`
- Pause → `PauseQueueCommand`
- Resume → `ResumeQueueCommand`

**Result Preview:**
- `ResultImageSource`, `HasResultImage`, `ImageInfo` bindings
- "Camera Edit", "Video Generator", "Open Folder" buttons

**For Image Analysis mode** (visible when `Analyzer.IsImageAnalysisMode`):

**Queue Status Bar:**
- `Analyzer.QueuedCount`, `Analyzer.CompletedCount`, `Analyzer.FailedCount`
- Progress when `Analyzer.IsProcessingQueue`

**Queue Items List:**
- `ItemsControl` bound to `Analyzer.QueueItems`
- Each item: workflow badge (`WorkflowBadge`, `WorkflowBadgeColor`), `DisplayPrompt`, `StatusDisplay`, `StatusColor`, progress, thumbnail, remove button
- Remove button: `Analyzer.RemoveFromQueueCommand` with CommandParameter binding

**Queue Controls:**
- Process Queue → `Analyzer.GenerateImageCommand`
- Clear Queue → `Analyzer.ClearQueueCommand`
- Pause → `Analyzer.PauseQueueCommand`
- Resume → `Analyzer.ResumeQueueCommand`
- Cancel → `Analyzer.CancelProcessingCommand`

**Result Preview:**
- `Analyzer.ResultImageSource`, `Analyzer.HasResultImage`, `Analyzer.ImageInfo`
- Open Output Folder → `Analyzer.OpenResultFolderCommand`

### Step 3: Keep the LM Studio connection settings
Add an Expander "LM Studio Connection" at the bottom of the Image Analysis settings section (visible only in Image Analysis mode), using the existing `Analyzer.LMStudioServer`, `Analyzer.LMStudioPort`, etc. bindings from the old Image Analysis tab. (Currently these are in the ImageAnalyzerWindow XAML, not in ImageGeneratorWindow — copy the pattern.)

### Step 4: Keep all other tabs unchanged
Tabs 3-7 (Story Image Z, Story Image Q, Story Image F, Amateur, Camera Angle) remain exactly as they are.

## 4. Visual Design Notes

- Use the same styles already defined in ImageGeneratorWindow.xaml Resources: `SectionPanelStyle`, `HeaderTextStyle`, `PrimaryButtonStyle`, `SecondaryButtonStyle`, `AnalyzeButtonStyle`
- Add the `ToggleRadioStyle` from `ImageAnalyzerWindow.xaml` (lines 123-155) to `ImageGeneratorWindow.xaml`'s Resources section
- Add the `QueueFlashAnimation` Storyboard from `ImageAnalyzerWindow.xaml` (lines 158-162) — but name the target border `AnalyzerQueueBorder` to avoid conflicts
- Queue items should use color-coded status: Blue=Queued, Orange=Processing, Green=Completed, Red=Failed
- Workflow badges: Z=purple, Q=blue, K=green (matching what's already in `ImageAnalyzerQueueItem.WorkflowBadgeColor`)

## 5. Key Binding Reference

### ImageGeneratorViewModel (direct bindings, no prefix):
- `ImagePrompt`, `SelectedWorkflow`, `AspectRatioIndex`, `Steps`, `Cfg`, `Seed`, `Denoise`
- `LoraEnabled`, `SelectedLora`, `AvailableLoras`, `RefreshLorasCommand`, `ShowLoraOptions`
- `GenerateImageCommand`, `CancelGenerationCommand`, `IsProcessing`, `ProcessingStatus`, `ProcessingProgress`, `ProgressPercentage`
- `ResultImageSource`, `HasResultImage`, `ImageInfo`, `OpenResultFolderCommand`
- `SendToCameraEditCommand`, `SendToVideoGeneratorCommand`
- `SavedPrompts`, `SelectedSavedPrompt`, `SavePromptCommand`, `DeletePromptCommand`
- `LogOutput`
- Queue: `PromptQueue`, `AddToQueueCommand`, `RemoveFromQueueCommand`, `ClearQueueCommand`, `ProcessQueueCommand`, `PauseQueueCommand`, `ResumeQueueCommand`, `IsProcessingQueue`, `IsQueuePaused`

### ImageAnalyzerViewModel (prefix with `Analyzer.`):
- `Analyzer.IsTextPromptMode`, `Analyzer.IsImageAnalysisMode`
- `Analyzer.SourceImagePath`, `Analyzer.BrowseImageCommand`, `Analyzer.SourceImageSource`, `Analyzer.HasSourceImage`
- `Analyzer.AnalyzeImageCommand`, `Analyzer.IsAnalyzing`
- `Analyzer.AnalysisText`, `Analyzer.SelectedWorkflowIndex`, `Analyzer.SelectedWorkflow`
- `Analyzer.AspectRatioIndex`, `Analyzer.Steps`, `Analyzer.Cfg`
- `Analyzer.ShowStyleOptions`, `Analyzer.StyleNames`, `Analyzer.SelectedStyleIndex`
- `Analyzer.ShowLoraOptions`, `Analyzer.LoraEnabled`, `Analyzer.SelectedLora`, `Analyzer.AvailableLoras`, `Analyzer.RefreshLorasCommand`
- `Analyzer.GenerateImageCommand`, `Analyzer.IsGenerating`, `Analyzer.ProcessingStatus`, `Analyzer.ProcessingProgress`, `Analyzer.ProgressPercentage`
- `Analyzer.ResultImageSource`, `Analyzer.HasResultImage`, `Analyzer.ImageInfo`, `Analyzer.OpenResultFolderCommand`
- Queue: `Analyzer.QueueItems`, `Analyzer.AddToQueueCommand`, `Analyzer.AddToQueueAndStartCommand`, `Analyzer.RemoveFromQueueCommand`, `Analyzer.ClearQueueCommand`, `Analyzer.CancelProcessingCommand`
- `Analyzer.QueuedCount`, `Analyzer.CompletedCount`, `Analyzer.FailedCount`
- `Analyzer.IsProcessingQueue`, `Analyzer.QueueProgress`, `Analyzer.QueueTotal`, `Analyzer.QueueProgressText`
- `Analyzer.PauseQueueCommand`, `Analyzer.ResumeQueueCommand`
- `Analyzer.LMStudioServer`, `Analyzer.LMStudioPort`, `Analyzer.SelectedModel`, `Analyzer.AvailableModels`, `Analyzer.RefreshModelsCommand`, `Analyzer.TestLMStudioConnectionCommand`
- Event: `Analyzer.QueueItemAdded`

## 6. Constraints
- **ONLY modify `ImageGeneratorWindow.xaml`** — all ViewModel code is already in place
- If code-behind changes are needed for the flash animation, also modify `ImageGeneratorWindow.xaml.cs` (subscribe to `Analyzer.QueueItemAdded` to trigger flash)
- Keep all other tabs (Story Image Z/Q/F, Amateur, Camera Angle) untouched
- Do NOT modify any ViewModel files
- Do NOT modify `ImageAnalyzerWindow.xaml` — it can remain as-is (standalone window backup)

## 7. Completion Instructions
Update this file with a "Changelog" section detailing:
- What XAML sections were added/removed
- Confirmation that the merged tab works with both input modes
- Confirmation that queue is visible and functional in both modes

